       t="An echocardiogram is an ultrasound of the heart, the same kind of scan used in pregnancy. It shows the heart's size and shape, how well it pumps, and how the valves open and close. It is painless and usually takes less than an hour. We use it when there is breathlessness, swelling, a murmur, or a suspected heart problem, or to follow a known condition. It answers a different question from the ECG: not the rhythm, but the structure and the pumping.",
       cue=["Ultrasound of the heart.", "Size, shape, pumping, valves.", "Painless, usually under an hour.", "Used for symptoms, murmur, known conditions."],
