       t="Is ninety over sixty too low? Not necessarily. A reading below ninety over sixty is commonly called low blood pressure. But the number alone does not tell us whether it is dangerous. A low reading with no symptoms, in someone whose pressure is usually low, is often fine. A reading that is not so low but comes with dizziness, fainting or confusion is a concern. So the answer to worry about the number, the symptoms, or both is: look at both, and look at what is normal for you.",
