       t="The symptoms that matter are dizziness or lightheadedness, fainting, blurred vision, weakness, tiredness, nausea, and confusion. Palpitations and headaches can also happen. One lower reading with no symptoms is usually not a cause for alarm. Persistent symptoms with low readings are different, and should be looked at. Keep a note of when the symptoms happen, what you were doing, and your readings. That record is very useful for your doctor.",
