       t="Dizziness on standing may be a postural drop, which doctors call orthostatic hypotension. Standing makes blood pool in the legs, and in some people the body does not adjust fast enough. In the clinic we check this. The person lies down for five minutes, and we measure blood pressure. Then they stand, and we measure again at one minute and at three minutes. A fall in the top number of twenty or more, or in the bottom number of ten or more, is abnormal. Dizziness during the test also counts. Please do not try this alone if you are unsteady. You could fall. It should be done in a clinic, with someone beside you.",
